LEECH LATTICE CONNECTION*
================================================================================

LEECH LATTICE CONNECTION  
The extended binary Golay code G₂₄ is the glue code of the Leech lattice Λ₂₄.

Key facts:

• Octads correspond to minimal vectors in Λ₂₄.  
• M₂₄ acts as a subgroup of Co₀, the full automorphism group of Λ₂₄.  
• The Monster group 𝕄 contains Co₀ as a subgroup.  
• Thus the large Witt design S(5,8,24) sits directly on the moonshine pathway:

G₂₄ → Λ₂₄ → Co₀ → 𝕄.

This is the bridge from Steiner systems to Monster Moonshine.
